From 3c270d73da2403af15c6577747c06082e329aa1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:59:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 011: fix geometry emulation NIR and the GS tiler DCD

Found by recording v6/v7 (G72, G52, G76) command buffers on a host debug
build under the panfrost drm-shim, with NIR validation and genxml asserts
on. All three are in the 007/008 code and also hit real geometry shaders:

- nir_if_phi() was given an else value built after nir_pop_if(), so a
  load_const sat before the phi in the merge block (invalid NIR) in
  load_indirect_inputs(), load_direct_bias() and the per-vertex input
  loads. The zeros are now built before the if.
- After the lowering the shader is COMPUTE, but it kept the geometry
  shader's xfb_info (NIR only allows it on VS/TES/GS) and the geometry
  info in the union that the compute info shares (garbage workgroup
  hints). The lowering now clears both.
- The tiler DRAW of a geometry draw packed Instance Primitive Size 0, a
  "padded" field that cannot encode 0 (assert in debug builds, a garbage
  value in release builds). It is 1 now.

Host check, recording only (the drm-shim cannot run kbase JM atoms):
transform feedback draws over all ten topologies, indexed and indirect
draws, counters, DrawIndirectByteCount, a geometry shader with xfb,
null descriptors and BC uploads, on PAN_GPU_ID 6221, 7212 and 7211;
valgrind shows no memory errors. biblioklept

